utton></td><td><b>Preview (Charon)</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">This episode follows a fast-moving story about a proposed charge on cargo passing through the Strait of Hormuz. We will look at the questions around the plan and follow the oil-price chart as the news develops.</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/preview.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="38.336">&#9654; 38.34s</button></td><td><b>Notification 2</b><br><small>voice=SFX</small></td><td class="txt">効果音(読み上げなし)</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="40.776">&#9654; 40.78s</button></td><td><b>Key phrases intro (Charon)</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">(共有固定Key phrases intro)</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="43.686">&#9654; 43.69s</button></td><td><b>Key Phrase 1</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">EN: give back<br>JA: 上がった分をいったん吐き出す</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/kp1_en.wav"></audio><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/kp1_ja_charon.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="51.476">&#9654; 51.48s</button></td><td><b>Key Phrase 2</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">EN: sea blockade<br>JA: 海からの封鎖</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/kp2_en.wav"></audio><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/kp2_ja_charon.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="59.396">&#9654; 59.40s</button></td><td><b>Key Phrase 3</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">EN: stand at center stage<br>JA: 注目の中心にある</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/kp3_en.wav"></audio><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/kp3_ja_charon.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="68.766">&#9654; 68.77s</button></td><td><b>Key Phrase 4</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">EN: take a sharp turn<br>JA: 事態が急に変わる</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/kp4_en.wav"></audio><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/kp4_ja_charon.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="77.636">&#9654; 77.64s</button></td><td><b>Key Phrase 5</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">EN: recover the cost<br>JA: かかった費用を回収する</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/kp5_en.wav"></audio><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/kp5_ja_charon.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="85.886">&#9654; 85.89s</button></td><td><b>Notification 3</b><br><small>voice=SFX</small></td><td class="txt">効果音(読み上げなし)</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="88.326">&#9654; 88.33s</button></td><td><b>Full story intro (Charon)</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">(共有固定Full story intro)</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="91.196">&#9654; 91.20s</button></td><td><b>Comment 1 (Charon)</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">Listen for what the 20% meant and what was still unclear about the plan.</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/comment_1.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="97.466">&#9654; 97.47s</button></td><td><b>Full Story Part 1 (Aoede)</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">This news feels like a short play in three acts. Act One was “20%.” Act Two brought an unexpected turn. Act Three was an unexpected move in oil prices.
46	
47	The curtain rose on July 13. At 10:16 a.m., Trump posted that the United States would seek a 20% charge on all cargo passing through the Strait of Hormuz. The aim was to recover the cost of US efforts to keep the strait safe.
48	
49	But “20%” was not a finished system. The post did not say who would pay, how the money would be collected, or what legal basis would support it. For the moment, only a large number stood at center stage.
50	
51	The number stayed at center stage for about a day. Then the story took a sharp turn.</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/full_story_part1.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="144.106">&#9654; 144.11s</button></td><td><b>Comment 2 (Charon)</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">So far, the key point is that the 20% charge was announced without clear details. Now, what happened to the plan the next day, and when did the oil-price rise occur?</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/comment_2.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="156.736">&#9654; 156.74s</button></td><td><b>Full Story Part 2 Heading (Aoede)</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">The 20% plan changes overnight</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/full_story_part2_heading.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="160.266">&#9654; 160.27s</button></td><td><b>Full Story Part 2 (Aoede)</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">About 24 hours and 48 minutes later, at 11:04 a.m. on July 14, Trump said the 20% plan would be replaced by trade and investment projects between Gulf states and the US. He cited “very productive discussions” with Middle Eastern leaders. He also said no one should charge ships in the Strait, and that he disliked fees.
52	
53	The change was sudden. But to read the oil move, the dates must be kept separate. On July 13, Brent rose 9.59% and settled at $83.30. Reuters linked that rise to concern about a US sea blockade of Iran, planned for the next day, and energy shipments through the Strait of Hormuz.</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/full_story_part2.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="203.746">&#9654; 203.75s</button></td><td><b>Comment 3 (Charon, Bridge to Part 3)</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">The 20% charge was announced, but important details were not clear. About a day later, the plan changed to trade and investment projects, while oil prices had already risen amid concern about a planned US sea blockade of Iran and energy shipments through the Strait. Next, listen for how the timing of that oil move fits into the story.</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/comment_3.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="224.636">&#9654; 224.64s</button></td><td><b>Full Story Part 3 Heading (Aoede)</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">The chart refuses to stay down</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/full_story_part3_heading.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="227.896">&#9654; 227.90s</button></td><td><b>Full Story Part 3 (Aoede)</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">On July 14, after the withdrawal and replacement announcement, Brent crude futures briefly gave back some of their gains. Soon, they returned close to the high level before the announcement. At the time of reporting, Brent was up about 2.6%, above $85 a barrel. Its final settlement price was $84.73, up 1.7% from the day before.</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/full_story_part3.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="254.766">&#9654; 254.77s</button></td><td><b>Comment 4 (Charon)</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">The story began with a proposed 20% charge, then changed quickly the next day. But oil prices did not simply return to where they started, so let’s bring the main point together now.</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/comment_4.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="267.516">&#9654; 267.52s</button></td><td><b>In One Line (Aoede)</b><br><small>voice=Charon</small></td><td class="txt">Concerns about US-Iran attacks, the sea blockade, and tanker safety continued on July 14, so the flashy 20% plan left the stage, but the chart only pulled back briefly before recovering: the policy turn and the oil chart’s “not over yet” movement happened on the same day.</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/b1b/narration/in_one_line.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_b1b" data-sec="285.886">&#9654; 285.89s</button></td><td>