62	The change was sudden. But the dates must stay separate to understand the oil move. On July 13, Brent rose 9.59% and settled at $83.30. Reuters linked that rise to concern about a US sea blockade of Iran. The blockade was planned for the next day. Reuters also linked it to energy shipments through the Strait of Hormuz.</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/a2/narration/full_story_part2.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_a2" data-sec="229.379">&#9654; 229.38s</button></td><td><b>Comment 3</b><br><small>voice=Aoede</small></td><td class="txt">ここまでで、ホルムズ海峡を通る貨物への20％の負担案が、約24時間後に米国との貿易・投資計画へ変わり、船に料金を求めない方針になったことを押さえてください。続いては、この急な変更の前後で、原油価格に何が起きたのかを聞いていきます。</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/a2/narration/comment_3.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_a2" data-sec="250.779">&#9654; 250.78s</button></td><td><b>Full Story Part 3 Heading</b><br><small>voice=Aoede</small></td><td class="txt">The chart refuses to stay down</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/a2/narration/full_story_part3_heading.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_a2" data-sec="254.603">&#9654; 254.60s</button></td><td><b>Full Story Part 3</b><br><small>voice=Aoede</small></td><td class="txt">After the withdrawal and replacement announcement, Brent crude futures briefly gave back some gains. Soon, they returned close to the high level before the announcement. At the time of reporting, Brent was up about 2.6%, above $85 a barrel. Its final settlement price was $84.73, up 1.7% from the day before.</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/a2/narration/full_story_part3.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_a2" data-sec="279.889">&#9654; 279.89s</button></td><td><b>Comment 4</b><br><small>voice=Aoede</small></td><td class="txt">ここまで、ホルムズ海峡を通る貨物に20％の負担を求める案が出たあと、湾岸諸国とアメリカの貿易や投資の計画に置き換えられた流れを見てきました。発表後、原油価格はいったん上げ幅を縮めましたが、その後は高い水準に戻りました。この流れを踏まえて、最後のまとめを英語で聞いてみましょう。</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/a2/narration/comment_4.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_a2" data-sec="305.089">&#9654; 305.09s</button></td><td><b>In One Line</b><br><small>voice=Aoede</small></td><td class="txt">Concerns about US-Iran attacks, the sea blockade, and tanker safety continued on July 14. So the flashy 20% plan left the stage. But the chart pulled back only briefly before recovering. The policy turn and the oil chart’s “not over yet” move happened that same day.</td><td><audio controls preload="none" src="file:///C:/Users/tensh/eigo-radio/er019_output/family_x_audio_production_wiring_01/family_x_b3_diversity_trial_01/hormuz__run_06_flashlite_full_kp/a2/narration/in_one_line.wav"></audio></td></tr><tr><td><button class="seek" data-target="episode_audio_a2" data-sec="325.637">&#9654; 325.64s</button></td><td><b>Outro</b><br><small>voice=SFX</small></td><td class="txt">音楽ジングル/固定音源(読み上げなし)。</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table>
